      "BG_minus_FG",
      "BG_only",
      "negative_FG",
      "negative_RCG",
      "bank_absence"
    ],
    "semantics": "fg_max/bg_max=max normalized Part1 query-reference similarity across reference coverage>=.5 / <.5. This is legacy pre-Part2 source cosine evidence, not the final host score. Each packet is checked against eight fixed token rows of cached FP16 q/r, max allowed difference .001; stored field is used without replacement.",
    "source_code": [
      "repo/demo_lists/demo9_transductive_ics/scripts/extent_experiment.py:111-118,168-178",
      "repo/demo_lists/demo9_transductive_ics/scripts/evidence_audit.py:198-210",
      "readout_sources/FoRIS_official.py:340-361"
    ],
    "source_verification": "Generator extracts actual Part1 maps; original FoRIS returns input unit maps or normalized position-debiased maps. cov comes only from reference mask resized by area. All feature audits occur without query-GT.",
    "data": "All existing exposed DEV220, old120/new100 reported separately. Not independent confirmation.",
    "evaluation": "Scores are token-constant on64. Exact original1024 D FP and TP pixel counts aggregate per16x16 token. Positive=FP that should be deleted, negative=TP that should survive. Primary within-episode AUC jointly conditions on independently computed RCG and FG quintiles among D-touched tokens; same25 cells for all scores. Also raw and RCG-only conditional AUC. Macro across common evaluable episodes, RandomState0 2000 photograph-group paired bootstrap.",
    "controls": "BG alone; negative FG alone, to distinguish genuine negative evidence from weak positive matching; negative RCG; one minus equal vote of all unique original64 candidate masks. Candidate absence is a diagnostic comparator only.",
    "decision": "No gate or mask before this first signal result; no threshold grid. An advantage needs consistency across batches and gain over negativeFG within RCGxFG bins.",
    "prior_distinction": "Prior reference RBF/linear filters acted on QMI additions. This fresh NN negative-evidence diagnostic acts only on conservative RCG deletions; it does not rename or rerun that addition filter.",
    "cost": "One CPU/BLAS/Torch thread. Cached packets, fields, masks, eight fixed query feature rows per episode; no GPU/download/fit."
